# DREAM-SURFACE-S2J checkpoint

## Result: visual gate failed, technical gate retained

The four requested Forward+ artifacts completed without new depth holes, transparent LOD overlap, or performance regression. The exclusive LOD and opaque/depth-prepass architecture remains technically valid.

The material-identity gate did not pass:

- object-space value and roughness breakup remains too subtle in the beauty views;
- bounded cortex windows are not legible in the required intact front/side/back views;
- the ecology continues to read as a red/magenta material family;
- the furnished colony placement is improved by a feeding mat but still lacks convincing optical separation between the mat and cellular body.

This packet is preserved as the failed S2J checkpoint. DREAM-COLOR-C1 begins from the technically clean S2I/S2J depth and LOD architecture, not from this color direction.

# DREAM-COLOR-C1 checkpoint

C1 established an approved governing color concept but failed human visual acceptance.
The packet is preserved unchanged as the baseline for C1B.

Observed visual failures:

- tissue reads as opaque beige/olive clay;
- process colors read as painted stripes;
- metamerism globally tints the render;
- crystal response reads as cyan transparent plastic;
- senescence changes value without destroying optical organization;
- furnished filament light collapses the organism into an orange lump.

C1B does not supersede this checkpoint or the unresolved S2J checkpoint.
